title: $:/plugins/tiddlywiki/hive/hive-images
caption: Hive images

This manager shows every image tiddler of the wiki and the copies that a save to Hive publishes. The ''hosted'' copy is uploaded to the image hoster of Hive and keeps the wiki light: the tiddler and the bodies that reference it store the url of the copy only. The ''on-chain'' copy is stored inside the replies of the wiki as base64 data and costs Hive Power (resource credits) to publish. A scaled or re-encoded copy is smaller and costs less, and with ''external only'' the hosted copy replaces it entirely.

Each preview shows the original next to the copy, and the sizes are known ''before'' anything is uploaded: the upload to the image hoster, and for the on-chain copy the number of parts that are posted and the share of the available Hive Power that they are estimated to cost. The share is read live from the Hive api with the price curve of the chain, so it works before the first save of this app; until the api answers, a save that was measured before gives the estimate instead. If a copy would use most of the remaining credits, the preview says so and the save would be stopped: scale it down first.

The settings of one image override the defaults in the control panel. A save uploads the hosted copies of the images that have ''upload on save'' ticked; the ''Upload'' button of an image uploads it immediately.

<$list filter="[type[image/jpeg]] [type[image/png]] [type[image/gif]] [type[image/webp]] [type[image/svg+xml]] +[sort[title]]" variable="imgTitle">

!!!<$view tiddler=<<imgTitle>> field="title"/>

|<$hive-imagepreview title=<<imgTitle>> dest="cdn"/> |<$hive-imagepreview title=<<imgTitle>> dest="chain"/> |
|!Hosted (images.hive.blog) |!On-chain (in the replies) |

;Hosted copy scale and quality
<$select tiddler=<<imgTitle>> field="hive-image-cdn-scale" default="1"><option value="1">100%</option><option value="0.75">75%</option><option value="0.5">50%</option><option value="0.25">25%</option></$select> <$select tiddler=<<imgTitle>> field="hive-image-cdn-quality" default="0.8"><option value="1">100%</option><option value="0.8">80%</option><option value="0.6">60%</option><option value="0.4">40%</option></$select>

;On-chain copy scale and quality
<$select tiddler=<<imgTitle>> field="hive-image-chain-scale" default="1"><option value="1">100%</option><option value="0.75">75%</option><option value="0.5">50%</option><option value="0.25">25%</option></$select> <$select tiddler=<<imgTitle>> field="hive-image-chain-quality" default="1"><option value="1">100%</option><option value="0.8">80%</option><option value="0.6">60%</option><option value="0.4">40%</option></$select>

<$checkbox tiddler=<<imgTitle>> field="hive-image-chain-external">External only, no copy on the chain</$checkbox>

<$checkbox tiddler=<<imgTitle>> field="hive-image-autoupload">Upload the hosted copy on save</$checkbox>

<$button><$action-hiveuploadimage title=<<imgTitle>>/>Upload</$button>

Hosted url: <$view tiddler=<<imgTitle>> field="hive-image-url"/>

---

</$list>

''Status:'' <$list filter="[[$:/state/tiddlywiki/hive/status]get[text]]" variable="ignore"><$text text=<<ignore>>/></$list>
